 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the 6 tests pass (the 4 existing ones plus the 2 new ones). I didn't add tests for the other fixes.\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** `monitor_flag_rate`, `pooled_flag_rate`, `flags_in_window`, `parse_transcript_log`, `dedupe_transcripts`, `daily_flag_counts` and `monitor_summary` now follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n  - **`flagged` parsing:** `1` gives True, `0` gives False and empty gives None. A `flagged` value other than those three raises `ValueError`, with the line number in the message. The SPEC doesn't cover that case, so I chose to raise.\n  - **Error line numbers:** `ValueError` messages give the 1-based line number, counting skipped lines.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test that `None` counts as not flagged (section 1) and a test that the last duplicate id wins (section 5).\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `flags_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries, and there is a new entry for `daily_flag_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** I fixed three more places where the code didn't follow the SPEC:\n  - `top_flagged_groups` now leaves out empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `flag_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and returns keys in sorted order.\n  - `longest_positive_streak` now resets the run when it hits a zero.\n\nI made `flags_in_window` return `0` for a negative `days`, which the SPEC doesn't specify.\n\nThe changes are in `safety_evals/loader.py`, `metrics.py` and `report.py`, plus `README.md` and `tests/test_metrics.py`.",
